build/
# Item 1.5 added -DALGO_SANITIZE=ON, which is built into a directory of its own
# so it never shadows the default build Phase 2 measures. `build/` does not
# match it — that pattern names one directory exactly.
build-*/

# Item 2.4 materialises each measured configuration as a git worktree here.
# They are build inputs, not sources: the tree inside one is exactly some
# commit already in this repository's history, and the build directory beside
# it is Linux GCC output produced inside the container. `git worktree list` is
# the record of which exist; this pattern only keeps them out of `git status`.
.worktrees/
cmake-build*
.idea/
.vs/
.DS_Store

# Working documents stay out of the repository — the roadmap, CLAUDE.md, the
# technical report, and any scratch notes dropped at the root. README.md is the
# single exception: it is the public face of the project.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose. `docs/` is deliberately NOT covered, because
# the roadmap requires docs/GRAMMAR.md (item 1.5), docs/BYTECODE.md (4.5) and
# docs/MEASUREMENT.md (2.1, 5.3) to be committed deliverables. Widening this to
# a bare `*.md` would silently ignore all three.
/*.md
!/README.md
TECHNICAL-REPORT.md